# Dynamic object-property panels

Read [DYNAMIC_PANELS.md](../../crates/atlas-shell/DYNAMIC_PANELS.md) before
changing selection strips, color/stroke editors, corner/wire capsules, or
dimension stringers. It is the approved visual owner, including the later
slender-capsule and short-stringer refinements; old A/B/C concepts are rejected.

Call or extend `atlas_shell::selection_tools`. Apps provide selection values
and journal actions; they do not paint substitute controls. For example,
Stroke uses the shared color editor with its extra width rail, not a copied
color form. Do not import dock pinning/stacked-inspector conventions into
object-attached editors.

The fillet capsule is the default capsule. Height is `CORNER_HEIGHT`
(1.3 × the 17-unit baseline), radius is half that height, stroke is 0.8,
and the fill is `theme.panel`. A thicker or thinner capsule is allowed only
when `DYNAMIC_PANELS.md` names it (wire baseline, photo-filter double height,
File Atlas formatting).

Keep behavior in P1.shape.properties and the selection contract. Use the
guide's native light/dark review procedure before claiming visual parity;
generated references and successful compilation are not runtime verification.
